The vulnerability is caused by a bug in the Linux kernel's pipe implementation. Pipes are used to communicate between processes. When a process writes data to a pipe, the data is stored in the pipe's buffer. The buffer is then read by the other process in the pipe.
The bug allows an attacker to write arbitrary data to arbitrary files by exploiting the pipe buffer. An attacker can create a pipe and then write data to the pipe. The data will be stored in the pipe's buffer. The attacker can then use the buffer to write the data to a different file.
